From 570b834b4dba8562db24770b8d44d9eafd0ccf55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:11:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard video startup and make theme backups portable

Guard the startup path reported in issue #685 by retaining the configured renderer while keeping video output disabled until a surface is attached. Reapply the no-surface guard before media loads.

Remove unsupported secondary subtitle font-size writes, avoid removing absent temporary crop filters, skip subtitle text queries without a selected track, and guard missing or invalid wallpaper files.

Save wallpapers as bounded Base64 PNG data in the existing preference and support legacy URI loading. Keep embedded images out of navigation state and filename labels. Stream PNG encoding to reduce temporary allocations.

Embed legacy wallpaper images in settings exports alongside custom theme colors, selection, and wallpaper adjustments. Version the backup format, preserve supplementary Unicode and string-set values, and stage complete XML exports before opening the destination.

Validate imports before committing preferences in one batch. Reject malformed values and invalid wallpapers, preserve cancellation, and count network imports only after insertion. Retain legacy backup import support and exclude device-bound network credentials.

Validation: scoped static source review, editor diagnostics, and git diff --check. No builds, tests, formatters, or device validation were run under the static-only constraint.
